From 32a6ad3aef859024ea2a7ceff32b57c48a3eff77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abel Vesa <abel.vesa@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:15:41 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 100/100] Revert "drm/msm/a8xx: Enable CLX feature on Adreno
 X2-85"

This reverts commit 93b6c8d10fad3d21a862d88d7187106aa6ecde8e.

With the CLX and IFF/PCLX limits tables sent to the GMU, the GPU fails
to initialize on Glymur CRD (and on the ASUS Zenbook A14 and Lenovo Yoga
Slim 7x as reported on the list): all CLX HFI messages are acked, but
the first HFI_H2F_MSG_GX_BW_PERF_VOTE after them never gets a reply and
the GMU stays wedged, with both GMU firmware v5.2.38 and v5.2.48.

Revert until the root cause is understood.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260516-a8xx-clx-support-v1-3-62508bf651ac@oss.qualcomm.com/
Signed-off-by: Abel Vesa <abel.vesa@oss.qualcomm.com>
